      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "Perfect! I found the answer. According to [[credential-scoping]]:\n\n**The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by using a local secrets loader that reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into the environment of spawned child processes (Ingest and Query agents) immediately before they start.** The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated with the key.\n\nThis approach means:\n- The key never exists in the Hub\u0027s environment variables\n- A compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment\n- The credential exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need to call the Anthropic API\n- Both the Ingest and Query agent processes receive the credential the same way \u2014 injected at spawn time, never inherited from the Hub",
      "input_tokens": 5359,
